:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=SAVDFT HELP=HLPDFT KEYL=PRMKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Specify Command Defaults
:TOPINST.Type choices, press Enter.
:DATA DEPTH='*'.
:DATAI VAR=DEV1 USAGE=INOUT.Devices
:DATAI VAR=DEV2 USAGE=INOUT.
:DATAI VAR=DEV3 USAGE=INOUT.
:DATAI VAR=DEV4 USAGE=INOUT.
:DATAI VAR=PMTCMD USAGE=INOUT.Prompt for commands
:DATAI VAR=CHKACT USAGE=INOUT.Check for active files
:DATAI VAR=MSGDLV USAGE=INOUT.Message queue delivery
:DATAI VAR=STRTIM USAGE=INOUT.Start time
:DATAI VAR=VRYOFF USAGE=INOUT.Vary off network servers
:DATAI VAR=UNMNT USAGE=INOUT.Unmount file systems
:DATAI VAR=PRTINF USAGE=INOUT.Print system information
:DATAI VAR=RPYL USAGE=INOUT.Use system reply list
:DATAI VAR=SPLDTA USAGE=INOUT.Spooled file data
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Y=Yes, N=No; delivery *BREAK or *NOTIFY; start time *CURRENT or HHMM
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=SAVCMDS HELP=HLPCMDS KEYL=PRMKEYS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Commands to Run
:TOPINST.These commands run in order. Press Enter to start them, F12 to return.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=CMDS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=CMDLINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPDSP.Display Backup Options - Help
:P.What the backup saves, where it puts it and how it runs. CHGBCKUP or
GO BACKUP option 10 changes the options; RUNBCKUP runs the backup.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPSTS.Display Backup Status - Help
:P.When each kind of data was last saved by a backup, and on which tape
set. F22 lists every backup that ran.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPHST.Display Backup History - Help
:P.The backups that ran, newest first: when, which option, the tape set
and whether only changed objects were saved. Option 5 shows the device,
whether every save completed and each save.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPDFT.Specify Command Defaults - Help
:P.The values the save or restore uses. Option 20 of GO SAVE keeps them
as the defaults the other options start from.
:P.Devices names up to four tape or optical devices; the first is used.
Prompt for commands shows each save before it runs. Check for active
files leaves a tape that still holds active files alone; N clears it.
The start time delays the run until then. Unmount, vary off, the
system reply list and the printed system information are done before
the first save.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPCMDS.Commands to Run - Help
:P.Ending the subsystems ends every job but this one. The last command
starts the controlling subsystem again.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
